WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.712
Welcome. This is your ten-day handwriting plan.

2
00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:09.374
The goal is simple to say. Every small letter starts in the right place, sits on the line, and can be read.

3
00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:16.413
It is the goal, not a promise. Day one and day ten are checks, and you put the pages side by side.

4
00:00:17.213 --> 00:00:20.594
This plan is for a child whose letters start at the bottom.

5
00:00:21.044 --> 00:00:23.961
Or come out in all sizes, and float off the line.

6
00:00:24.411 --> 00:00:25.686
Or face the wrong way.

7
00:00:26.136 --> 00:00:30.351
And for the child who finds writing so tiring that it ends in tears.

8
00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:37.066
Hands grow into writing. At four and five, wobbly letters are common. They are not a problem to fix.

9
00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:41.202
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day.

10
00:00:41.652 --> 00:00:48.007
On day one your child writes a short sample, and you watch the pencil. On day ten they write it again.

11
00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:53.714
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

12
00:00:54.164 --> 00:00:59.333
And every small letter in the book has a green dot. The dot shows where the pencil starts.

13
00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:02.448
Like this one. Start at the top. Pull down.

14
00:01:04.154 --> 00:01:09.385
Your child says those words out loud while writing. The words are what the hand remembers.

15
00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:17.764
Now, what to expect. Day two is not letters at all. It is how to sit, how to hold the pencil, and how the paper lies.

16
00:01:18.214 --> 00:01:24.907
Then one family of letters a day. Letters in a family start the same way, so one move teaches many letters.

17
00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:30.190
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

18
00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.669
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

19
00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.915
This plan teaches the small letters in print. No capitals, and no cursive.

20
00:01:39.715 --> 00:01:46.202
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

21
00:01:46.652 --> 00:01:51.221
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

22
00:01:51.671 --> 00:01:54.818
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

23
00:01:55.268 --> 00:02:01.427
Then your child carries on with the page, circles their own best letter, and shows you three things at the end.

24
00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:06.756
On three of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

25
00:02:07.556 --> 00:02:12.552
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and three crayons: blue, yellow and red.

26
00:02:13.002 --> 00:02:16.744
When you are ready, start with day one. It takes about three minutes.
